cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GPS-VDI: visual diversity of flying insects from sticky-trap scans"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the dataset it analyses."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Keasar
    given-names: Chen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0994-1520"
    affiliation: "Ben-Gurion University of the Negev"
  - family-names: Cabra-Leykin
    given-names: Liraz
    affiliation: "Ben-Gurion University of the Negev"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/chenKeasar/gps-vdi"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a method that estimates the diversity of flying insects directly from
  scanned yellow sticky traps, without identifying the specimens. Each detected arthropod
  is reduced to five visual features; the spread of those features across a trap is
  summarised by a grid-based entropy estimator, giving a per-trap visual diversity index.
keywords:
  - insect biodiversity
  - sticky traps
  - image analysis
  - entropy estimation
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Insect biodiversity assessment"
    doi: "10.17632/6pbgs93kdf"
    authors:
